repl_show — evaluation
=======================

status: planned (2026-07-09)
focal tool: repl_show (plans/repl_show)

task
----
review one repl's full history — the "what have I done so far"
question, as opposed to repl_state's "what is the goal at idx".

setup
-----
harness pre-creates repl "review" with ~6 steps, one of which was
preceded by failed attempts (invisible in history — failures leave
no trace; that fact is part of what the output teaches).

prompt
------
"Walk me through the proof attempt named 'review': list the steps
taken so far in order, and note where the proof currently stands."

success
-------
all steps reported in order plus a correct tip status; no mutating
calls.

signals
-------
- repl_show vs repl_text vs repeated repl_state: three plausible
  routes. which reads as "the history view"? if repl_text (source
  only, no states) wins, the show/text split may not be legible from
  the descriptions.
- if the harness manages to present "review" busy on first call:
  does the "busy" error route the agent to repl_list (the documented
  busy-safe overview) or to a retry loop?

reflection
----------
- show/state/text form a triad with overlapping surfaces; if
  transcripts show agents using them interchangeably or always
  chaining all three, spec question: merge or sharpen the
  descriptions' contrast ("show = steps, state = one goal, text =
  paste-ready source").
